{"packet_id":"D079-01","doc_id":"D079","jurisdiction":"San Francisco, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"San Francisco Rent Ordinance just cause eviction requirement","requirement":"A landlord may evict a tenant from a rental unit covered by the Rent Ordinance only for one of the 17 just cause reasons in Section 37.9(a); expiration of the rental agreement or a change of ownership is not just cause.","key_value":"17 just cause reasons under § 37.9(a)","coverage_conditions":"Rental units covered by the Rent Ordinance; tenancies exempt from the Ordinance's rent increase limits, including units first certified for occupancy after June 13, 1979, remain subject to the eviction provisions.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Tenancies in units first certified for occupancy after June 13, 1979, tenancies eligible for a Costa-Hawkins rent increase, and some tenancies whose rent another agency regulates stay subject to the eviction provisions.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"A landlord who evicts or tries to evict a tenant unlawfully may face substantial civil and/or criminal liability.","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"S.F. Admin. Code § 37.9","quoted_span":"In order to evict a tenant from a rental unit covered by the Rent Ordinance, a landlord must have a \"just cause\" reason that is the dominant motive for pursuing the eviction.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D079-01","doc_id":"D079","jurisdiction":"San Francisco, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"San Francisco Rent Ordinance rent increase limit exemptions","requirement":"The Rent Ordinance's rent increase limitations do not apply to tenancies in newly constructed units first certified for occupancy after June 13, 1979, to tenancies eligible for a Costa-Hawkins increase, or to some tenancies whose rent another agency regulates.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental units under the Rent Ordinance, apart from the listed exempt tenancies.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"built","role":"exempt","op":"after","date":"1979-06-13","basis":"certificate_of_occupancy"}],"per_tenancy":"Tenancies eligible for a rent increase under the Costa-Hawkins Rental Housing Act and some tenancies whose rent is regulated by another government agency.","coverage_quotes":["Some tenancies that are exempt from the rent increase limitations of the Ordinance are still subject to the eviction provisions of the Ordinance, and tenants in these categories can only be evicted for one of the “just cause” reasons listed in the Ordinance."]},"exemptions":"Tenancies in units first certified for occupancy after June 13, 1979; tenancies eligible for a rent increase under the Costa-Hawkins Rental Housing Act; some tenancies whose rent is regulated by another government agency.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"S.F. Admin. Code ch. 37","quoted_span":"This includes tenancies in newly constructed rental units that first obtained a Certificate of Occupancy after June 13, 1979, tenancies that are eligible for a rent increase under the Costa-Hawkins Rental Housing Act, and some tenancies where the rent is regulated by another government agency.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.6,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D079-01","n_rules":2,"note":null}

